<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  OPTIONAL - form-factor product trees.

  Not part of the numbered tiers, and not installed by tools/init.sh.
  Copy it into .repo/local_manifests/ only if you are certain you want a
  phone-only tree.

  What these actually are
  -----------------------
  These are not hardware support. They are the product definitions for
  entire form factors, and each carries lunch targets:

    device/google/atv       aosp_tv_arm64, aosp_tv_x86, gsi_tv_arm64,
                            gsi_tv_arm, sdk_atv64_arm64, sdk_atv_x86
                            plus the atv_* layering stack: atv_base,
                            atv_system, atv_system_ext, atv_product,
                            atv_vendor, atv_generic_system

    device/generic/car      gsi_car_arm64, gsi_car_x86_64,
                            sdk_car_arm64, sdk_car_x86_64,
                            sdk_car_md_arm64, sdk_car_md_x86_64,
                            sdk_car_cw_x86_64

    device/google_car       Google car reference device

  Why you might want to keep them
  -------------------------------
  The atv_* stack is the only worked example in AOSP of a form factor
  layered cleanly on base_system - atv_system.mk sits beside
  handheld_system.mk and does the same job for a different device class.
  If you are adding a form factor that AOSP does not ship (Wear OS is
  proprietary and absent; there is no desktop product), that stack is
  the template you would copy.

  What is NOT here
  ----------------
  The applications and services for these form factors live elsewhere
  and are never pruned by this repository:

    platform/packages/services/Car          the Automotive service
    platform/packages/apps/Car/*            29 Automotive applications
    platform/frameworks/opt/car/services
    platform/packages/apps/TV, TvSettings, TvSystemUI
    platform/packages/providers/TvProvider
    platform/frameworks/opt/tv/tvsystem
    platform/packages/inputmethods/LeanbackIME

  Removing the product trees below without also removing those leaves
  the code in place and only the lunch targets gone.

  Verified against android-15.0.0_r20.

  Saving: ~1 GB
  Risk:   high if you later want TV or Automotive - you lose the targets
-->
<manifest>
  <remove-project name="device/google/atv" />
  <remove-project name="device/generic/car" />
  <remove-project name="device/google_car" />
</manifest>
